v1 (final -- distributional verdict passed 2026-07-28)

The engine formerly "smax78-v82" (tagged v0), rewritten so the whole solver
is inspectable: one insertion algorithm, one prefilter semantic per role,
zero dead knobs, kernel 1594 lines, every line reachable. Validated
DISTRIBUTIONALLY against a same-toolchain v0 rebuild (3 portfolio seeds x
full-40 @T300 each, plus T900):

  quality    3-seed means: v1 -0.71% (parity; medians ~0)
  variance   seed-to-seed per-instance spread ~9-10% both engines
  tail       v0 collapsed prob_29 to _trivial (1.53e9, ~4000x) in 2 of 5
             draws; v1: zero collapses in 5 draws -- the hardened gate
             (nudge -> retime -> tight/loose move, deadline-aware, seed
             floor) removed the failure mode
  canary     prob_1 1499 / prob_2 3690 preserved
  anneal     +32% iterations, -2.9% quality from identical seeds (controlled)

Single-draw A/Bs between engine families compare lottery tickets, not
engines: a kernel change reshuffles the RNG stream once, and the fixed
portfolio seed then freezes that redraw (v1c/v1d/v1e produced byte-identical
objectives on the same instances). Judge engine changes on multi-seed
distributions (OGC_SEED) or accept only differences far outside the ~10%
per-instance draw band.

Deliberate deviations from v0, each measured: unified seeder path (seed A/B
40/40: parity), post-compaction portfolio merge (strictly better-informed),
8 destroyer slots (mixture drift real but quality-neutral), crane-aware
hits() kept in the dense fallback as placement policy, gate ladder +
reserve + seed floor (the robustness win), OGC_DIAG/OGC_SEED env hooks
(inert on the grading server).
